# Windows batch files MUST be checked out with CRLF line endings.
# cmd.exe can mis-parse LF-only .bat files (goto labels and parenthesised
# blocks are the usual casualties), and this repo is authored on macOS --
# so pin it here instead of relying on each user's core.autocrlf setting.
# Applies to `git clone` and to GitHub's "Download ZIP" alike.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Everything else: keep LF in the repo, let git decide on checkout.
*.py   text
*.md   text
*.yaml text
*.js   text
*.html text
*.htm  text

# Binary-ish artefacts should never be line-ending-converted.
*.png  binary
*.har  binary
